# Brand guidelines — doihave.space

Read `brand-guidelines/` before writing or editing marketing, editorial, or UI copy on matched paths.

## Canonical docs

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `brand-guidelines/tone-of-voice.md` | Voice, adjectives, disclaimer tiers, naming, visual voice |
| `brand-guidelines/product-features.md` | Feature headlines, coverage matrix, out-of-scope claims |
| `brand-guidelines/customer-pain-points.md` | Persona × pain × message × CTA |
| `brand-guidelines/style-references.md` | Annotated in-app copy seeds |
| `brand-guidelines/copy-prompts.md` | Prompt skeletons — use when user asks for marketing copy |

Manual `@brand-guidelines` works outside these globs.

## Hard boundaries

- **Statute / regulations:** `src/lib/regulations/` — cited claims, disclaimers, briefing prose (Regulations Expert agent). Components render only.
- **Commercial / editorial:** `src/lib/content/` — affiliates, guides corpus, premium catalog.
- **Never mix** affiliate marketing into statute data or invent eligibility in copy.

## Voice essentials

- Institutional, precise, architectural — not hype.
- Fixed status vocabulary: **Eligible** / **Warning** / **Restricted** (never "approved" or "denied").
- Coverage honesty: lot GIS only where providers cover the coordinate; jurisdiction fallback is normal, not an error.
- Reframe "loopholes" as lawful pathways, not permit dodges.

## Disclaimer tiers

| Tier | When |
|------|------|
| Full | Guides, regulations, receipts |
| Short | Footer, compact UI |
| Commercial | Affiliates (`AFFILIATE_DISCLOSURE`) |
| Matching | Connect / builder match |

## Outcome CTAs (with product-role.mdc)

| `overall` | Primary | Avoid |
|-----------|---------|-------|
| eligible | Outfit the build / partners | Rose "Request Review" |
| warning | Amber specialist review | Full shop grid above form |
| restricted | Rose expert compliance review | Shop grid above lead form |

## When user requests copy

Use the skeleton in `brand-guidelines/copy-prompts.md`: Goal, Format, Audience, Tone, Constraints, Context, Do not.
